Treat this target as the BSD-like platform it is

`-target x86_64-unknown-freebsd` defines `__FreeBSD__`, so `StormPort.h` takes its
Linux/BSD branch - and that branch is right about almost everything and wrong
about two things. Both are corrected here rather than worked around outside,
because the file's job is to say what the platform has.

**mmap: claimed, absent.** The branch includes `<sys/mman.h>` and defines
`STORMLIB_HAS_MMAP` for every BSD-derived platform. There is no mmap here, so the
include fails and all thirty sources stop at it.

Faking it would be worse than declining. The obvious shim - read the file into a
buffer, return the pointer - turns a memory-mapped read into a full load, and
Ocarina of Time's `.otr` is hundreds of megabytes. Nothing is lost by saying no:
the path is guarded (`FileStream.cpp:572` is an `#elif` whose `#else` at :605
returns "File mapping is not supported") and libultraship never asks for it -
`OtrArchive.cpp:71` calls `SFileOpenArchive` with `MPQ_OPEN_READ_ONLY` and no
`STREAM_PROVIDER_MAP`, so archives come through the ordinary file stream.

**The 64-bit calls: absent, and present.** The branch expects Linux's large-file
names - `stat64`, `fstat64`, `lseek64`, `ftruncate64`, `off64_t` - which exist
because Linux once had a 32-bit `off_t`. FreeBSD never did, so it has the plain
names and no aliases, and `FileStream.cpp` stops on an incomplete `struct
stat64`.

StormLib already handles exactly this for macOS, four lines lower, for exactly
the same reason - "64-bit calls are supplied by normal calls on Mac". This joins
that condition rather than adding a second copy of it, and picks up its
`O_LARGEFILE 0` while it is there.

Both are guarded on `__PROSPERO__`, so every other platform keeps what upstream
gave it, and the conditions still read as upstream's.

diff --git a/src/StormPort.h b/src/StormPort.h
index aa2c9f5..741e460 100644
--- a/src/StormPort.h
+++ b/src/StormPort.h
@@ -306,7 +306,7 @@
   #endif
 
   // Platforms with mmap support
-  #if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__DragonFly__)
+  #if (defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__DragonFly__)) && !defined(__PROSPERO__)
     #include <sys/mman.h>
     #define STORMLIB_HAS_MMAP
   #endif
@@ -387,7 +387,7 @@
 #endif // !STORMLIB_WINDOWS
 
 // 64-bit calls are supplied by "normal" calls on Mac
-#if defined(STORMLIB_MAC)
+#if defined(STORMLIB_MAC) || defined(__PROSPERO__)
   #define stat64  stat
   #define fstat64 fstat
   #define lseek64 lseek
